        <tbody>
          {ranked.map((o) => (
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 align-top">
              <td class="py-3 pr-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">{o.rank}<div class="font-normal text-gray-500 whitespace-nowrap">{o.total} of 9</div></td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">
                <a href={`#${o.id}`} class="font-semibold text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">{o.name}</a>
                <div class="text-gray-500">{o.channels}</div>
              </td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-gray-700"><strong class="text-gray-900">{o.sellScore}</strong> {o.sell}</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-gray-700"><strong class="text-gray-900">{o.priceScore}</strong> {o.price}</td>
              <td class="py-3 text-gray-700"><strong class="text-gray-900">{o.accessScore}</strong> {o.access}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 prose prose-lg max-w-3xl">
      <h2>Which option fits your channel</h2>

      <p>The ranking mixes channels, so pick the highest-ranked option that works for yours.</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Newsletter on beehiiv or Kit.</strong> Try the built-in network first: beehiiv Scale is from $43 a month billed yearly, Kit Creator from $33 a month billed yearly with Kit keeping 23.5% of ad revenue.</li>
        <li><strong>Newsletter on any platform.</strong> Sponsor Radar emails brands for you at 10¢ per email after $20 in credits, while Hecto (5%) and MediaPact (10%) list your slots and wait for brands to book.</li>
        <li><strong>YouTube channel in the Partner Program.</strong> The Creator Partnerships tab in YouTube Studio lists no fee and shows up automatically for eligible channels in listed countries.</li>
        <li><strong>Podcast.</strong> Libsyn Ads needs 20,000 downloads per episode and lets you keep 70%. Below that, MediaPact, Passionfroot and Sponsorships.ai publish no minimum.</li>
        <li><strong>Short-form video or UGC.</strong> Collabstr's listings are mostly Instagram, TikTok and UGC, and creators pay a 15% fee on their payout.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Each option in rank order</h2>
    </div>

